/* ============================================================================
   EKG EXPLORER — SDVsolution Engineering Knowledge Graph (prototype)
   ============================================================================

   WHAT THIS IS
   ------------
   A single-file React prototype that treats the ~1,271 L1 system requirements
   as the ONLY true input and GENERATES every downstream engineering artifact
   from them in code: L0 groupings, use cases, architecture + ECU allocation,
   interfaces/signals, software requirements, verification, and the safety
   (HARA/ASIL), cybersecurity (TARA) and reliability (FMEA) analyses.

   WHY GENERATE INSTEAD OF STORE
   -----------------------------
   Keeping the derivation rules in the tool (not in a spreadsheet) means every
   view is always consistent and there is one place to change a rule. Derived
   values are never persisted — e.g. RPN = Severity x Occurrence x Detection is
   recomputed on read, so editing severity moves RPN everywhere it appears.

   DATA FLOW (top to bottom in this file)
   --------------------------------------
     1. RAW_GRAPH / EXEC / ASPICE      injected JSON (real master-data slice)
     2. heuristics + generators        classify an L1, emit downstream nodes/edges
     3. NETWORK + buildGraph           base graph = L1s + ECUs + normalized I/O
     4. {CCU,CCM,CZM,FZM}_IO           per-ECU interface lists (from the ICDs)
     5. genL2 / generateDownstream     lazy 1->many decomposition + artifacts
     6. computeReadiness               dashboard rollups
     7. engines (HARA/TARA/FMEA)       parameter-driven classifications
     8. layout + components            graph layout and node rendering
     9. App()                          state, navigation history, and all views

   LAZY GENERATION
   ---------------
   The base graph holds only L1s, ECUs and I/O. Downstream artifacts (and L2s)
   are materialized on demand when a requirement is focused, so the graph stays
   small until you explore it.

   HONEST CAVEATS
   --------------
   The keyword classifiers and the seeded S/E/C, Impact/Feasibility and Occ/Det
   values are CANDIDATES ("proposed, pending workshop"), not signed-off
   assessments. The engines do the standard math correctly; a human confirms the
   inputs. All edits live in-session only (no persistence/undo) — that belongs to
   a system-of-record backend.

   BUILD PIPELINE
   --------------
   Authoring happens in template.jsx; a Python step injects the JSON in place of
   the GRAPH / EXEC / ASPICE data placeholders to produce the shipped .jsx.
   ============================================================================ */

import React, { useState, useMemo, useRef, useEffect, useCallback } from "react";
import {
  ChevronRight, ChevronLeft, ChevronDown, ChevronUp, Search, X, Plus, Minus, Maximize2,
  GitBranch, Table, Share2, BookOpen, AlertTriangle, Filter, Lock,
  Copy, FolderPlus, Check, Package, Layers, Pencil,
  ArrowLeftRight, ArrowLeft, ArrowRight, Sparkles, Send, Download, Upload, FileDown, FileUp, Trash2, MessageSquarePlus, ExternalLink, Cpu, UserRound, Workflow, Home,
} from "lucide-react";

